// Chapter 1 — the camp. Shows a hub (@hub) whose options are storylets tagged "camp".

=== camp.arrival
@title Base Camp

{image("camp-art", "A riverside expedition camp with canvas tents and supplies at the edge of dense jungle.")}

The boat leaves {player:first-name} at the edge of the jungle with a pack, a {item:torch#lower} and
three weeks of unanswered letters. The {faction:explorers-guild:name} has given {player:pronoun#object}
one season to find the **{item:relic}** before they hand the expedition to someone more *reliable*.

> guide: {player:name}. You're later than your letter promised. I'm {guide:first-name} — the guild sent me.

{player:last-name#possessive} reputation for punctuality is, {player:pronoun} {player:pronoun#one-many("has", "have")} to admit, deserved.

-> camp.hub

=== camp.hub
@title The Camp
@hub camp

The camp hums with insects. {guide:first-name} sharpens a machete by the fire{if var:supplies > 0}, eyeing the supplies
you bought{/if}.

* [Set out for the temple] -> trail.river

=== camp.supplies
@title Haggle for supplies
@tags camp
@once
@priority 10
@hub all(camp,records)

{image("expedition-workshop", "A sheltered camp worktable holds a rucksack, rations, rope and expedition records beside a hanging watch bell.")}

~ var:ledger = (6 + 2) * 3 / 2 - 1
~ var:ledger -= 1

A trader with a gold tooth unrolls a blanket of goods. You come away with a {item:rope#lower} and a
{item:charm#lower} he swears keeps the river spirits polite.
Two {item:ration}s complete the bargain. The trader checks the expedition slate:
`((6 + 2) * 3 / 2 - 1) - 1` is **{var:ledger}** crates, enough to supply the camp.

~ give player rope
~ give player charm
~ give player ration 2
~ set flag:packing-open
~ var:supplies += 2

{if var:ledger == 10 and var:ledger != 0}
The accounts balance. All that remains is to check the register.
{/if}

-> camp.hub

=== camp.register
@title Sign the expedition register
@tags camp,records
@once
@priority 10

The clerk writes **{player:name#upper}**, then carefully corrects the entry to
{player:name}. The margin says: "{player:pronoun#capitalize} signed
{player:pronoun#possessive} own name; this copy is {player:pronoun#possessive("independent")}.
Ask {player:pronoun#object} to check it {player:pronoun#reflexive}."

{item:idol#a#capitalize} decorates the clerk's stamp. Its label reads \{expedition copy\}.

> guide: I use {guide:pronoun}/{guide:pronoun#object}. Names matter more than the guild admits.

-> camp.hub

=== camp.guide
@title Ask your guide about the temple
@tags camp
@once

> guide: The old ones built it to keep something *in*, not people out. The guild knows that. They never write it down.

{guide:first-name} tells you about the river crossing, and about the explorer who went in last spring and came out
talking only in numbers.

{if faction:explorers-guild >= friendly}
> guide: The guild speaks well of you. I'll do what I can.
{else}
> guide: Between us, the guild expects you to fail.
{/if}

~ faction:explorers-guild += 5
-> camp.hub

=== camp.journal
@title Study your journal
@tags camp
@once
@priority 5

You spread {player:pronoun#possessive} {item:journal} across your knees. The glyph rubbings from the museum
are smudged, but a pattern repeats: *a spiral, a closed eye, a hand.*

* [Puzzle out the glyphs] skill-check history dc 12
  success: { set flag:knows-glyphs; player:xp += 50; player:lucidity += 2 } -> camp.journal-solved
  failure: -> camp.journal-failed

=== camp.journal-solved
It's a warning and an instruction at once: *follow the spiral to the hand, and the stone will open the way.*
You underline it twice. The pattern settles into focus; your Lucidity rises to **{player:lucidity}**.
-> camp.hub

=== camp.journal-failed
The marks blur into each other. You close the journal with a headache and nothing else.
-> camp.hub

// Text state: an explicit manifest default, a hoisted Talemark declaration, copied values,
// equality/inequality, empty text and literal assignments on choices.
=== camp.watchword
@title Agree on a night watchword
@tags camp
@once

~ var:watch-note = ""

> guide: If we lose each other after dark, call the watchword. Tonight's suggestion is "{var:watchword}".

{if var:watch-note == ""}
The watch ledger has no phrase recorded yet.
{/if}

* [Keep quiet river] -> camp.watchword-record
* [Use silver heron instead] { var:watchword = "silver heron" } -> camp.watchword-record

=== camp.watchword-record
@title A Note for the Night Watch

~ var:watch-note = var:watchword

You write **{var:watch-note}** in the watch ledger. {guide:first-name} asks what should happen
if a stranger overhears it.

* [Change the watchword to lantern light] (requires: var:watchword == var:watch-note) { var:watchword = "lantern light" } -> camp.watchword-readback
* [Retire the watchword without a replacement] (requires: var:watchword == var:watch-note) { var:watchword = "" } -> camp.watchword-readback
* [Keep the recorded watchword] (requires: var:watchword == var:watch-note) -> camp.watchword-readback

=== camp.watchword-readback
@title Ink Does Not Follow Orders

{if var:watchword == ""}
> guide: No watchword tonight, then. Stay within sight of the fire.
{else}
> guide: The current watchword is "{var:watchword}". Remember it, not the old one.
{/if}

{if var:watch-note != var:watchword}
The ledger still reads **{var:watch-note}**. Changing the spoken watchword did not
rewrite the ink: the note holds a copy, not a promise to follow later changes.
{/if}

* [Close the watch ledger] -> camp.hub
